<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 2 November, from 1783 to 2000.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1783 CE <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington issues his farewell orders to the Continental Army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From Rocky Hill, New Jersey, George Washington issued his Farewell Orders to the Armies of the United States. Weeks later he resigned his commission, setting a precedent of civilian control.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1889 CE <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">North and South Dakota become US states</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Benjamin Harrison signed proclamations admitting North and South Dakota on the same day. He shuffled the papers so no one would know which was signed first.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Balfour Declaration backs a Jewish home in Palestine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Foreign Secretary Arthur Balfour wrote to Lord Rothschild that Britain favoured 'a national home for the Jewish people' in Palestine, without prejudice to existing non-Jewish communities. Its consequences still shape the region.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1930 CE <span class="tih-ago">96 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Haile Selassie is crowned Emperor of Ethiopia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ras Tafari Makonnen was crowned Emperor Haile Selassie I in Addis Ababa before foreign dignitaries. He ruled Ethiopia, with an interruption during Italian occupation, until his overthrow in 1974.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1936 CE <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The BBC launches the world's first regular high-definition TV service</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From Alexandra Palace in north London, the BBC began a regular public television service in what was then called high definition. It was suspended during the Second World War and resumed in 1946.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2000 CE <span class="tih-ago">26 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first crew moves into the International Space Station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Expedition 1, an American astronaut and two Russian cosmonauts, docked at the International Space Station. Since then the station has been continuously occupied by humans.</p></div></li></ol>
